module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.body_producer_work_is_not_bounded_by_its_declared_input

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data body_producer_work_is_not_bounded_by_its_declared_input: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "body_producer_work_is_not_bounded_by_its_declared_input" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a body producer's work is not bounded by its DECLARED INPUT. The producer owns a construct and a captured subtree; the work it actually performs is a function of some larger population -- enclosing structure, sibling declarations, or the whole file -- and nothing states or checks the denominator. The class is named for the missing BOUND rather than for a mechanism, because several mechanisms produce it: re-entry into a general walker, a deep search standing in for a direct slot read, or a fallback sequence that inspects unrelated structure before refusing. Which one applies to any given specimen is a finding, not part of the identity.",

    "THE DISTINGUISHING OBSERVATION, and it is what separates this from ordinary slowness: cost tracks a population the producer does not own. Observed here as the size and depth of the containing file predicting the cost while the count of the construct the producer is about does not. A file with 16 function literals stalls while a file with 61 completes; the three that stall are the three largest and deepest members of the closure, above roughly 200k parse nodes and depth 580, against members at roughly 58k nodes and depth 227 that finish. A cost that tracked the owned population would track the construct count. It tracks the enclosure instead.",

    "A CANDIDATE MECHANISM, NOT AN ESTABLISHED ONE, recorded so the experiment that would settle it is obvious. These parse trees are spine-dominated: every grammar production adds a level, so median depth across the closure is 145 and the maximum is 979 for source whose authored nesting is about 8. A producer whose work were per-ancestor rather than per-node would therefore be multiplied by a factor that has nothing to do with what the author wrote, and invisible in any specimen small enough to review by hand. DEPTH IS A CORRELATE IN THE OBSERVED POPULATION AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED AS THE CAUSAL VARIABLE: the three stalling members are also the three largest by node count, so size and depth are not separated by this evidence. An operation-count series over fixed-shape specimens -- flat/wide against deep spine, at 1k/2k/4k/8k nodes -- separates them; until it runs, neither is the mechanism.",

    "RECEIPT, 2026-09-25, gunbc#12210 merged onto the demand-engine head. The function-value change CLEARS the selected seven-test semantic wall -- a function value acquires a real lowered form, which is a genuine safety climb and must not be reverted into the silent narrowing it replaced. On the same head the full 133-file native context emitted NO per-file split row in 55 minutes at 99.7% CPU with flat resident memory, so the route that exists to reach the seven could not reach them. `dag.dag` completed under 25 minutes, which rules out non-termination and establishes nothing about asymptotic shape.",

    "TWO CLAIMS THAT WERE WITHDRAWN, RECORDED BECAUSE THE WITHDRAWAL IS THE LESSON. A regression FACTOR of 33x was reported and retracted: the pre-change figure was normalize time from a full-closure route run and the post-change figure was an isolated single-file census, which is two modes over two populations rather than a comparison. And the terminal refusal was reported as evidence that the expensive path explores unrelated structure before refusing; a file censused ALONE has none of its imports present, so that refusal is not controlled for isolation. Both readings were internally consistent and neither was anchored, which is the failure mode of a measurement whose baseline was never taken the same way.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, and only by a human noticing a route did not finish. The invalid state is fully writable, no check bounds a producer's visited-node count against its owned population, and nothing reports work amplification -- the route's own cost partition measures spans, which report that a phase was slow and never that a traversal was re-entered.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED. Owned population and visited count are both derivable at the producer, so a producer that visits each owned semantic node a bounded number of times can be admitted by construction rather than measured after the fact. It is not structurally IMPOSSIBLE while a producer may still call a general walker at all, which is why the trigger below names the consumption discipline rather than a prohibition.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY: every body producer consumes its DECLARED CAPTURED SLOTS and visits each node in its OWNED semantic population a derived, bounded number of times, and unrelated enclosing or sibling populations do not enter the work denominator. A timeout, a memo over the repeated search, or a cache at the link where the slowness was measured retires nothing -- the first converts an unbounded traversal into a policy, and the other two make redundant work cheap and suppress the signal that would make it rank for deletion (DESIGN section 2 and section 6b). The rows that carry this are V2-BODY-COST-0 through 3 in gunbc.plans.discrete_cost_derivation section 16.",

    "WHAT IS EXPLICITLY NOT THIS CLASS: `symptom_link_patched_without_the_earliest_unjustified_boundary` is the adjacent row and describes the REPAIR going wrong -- a guard or cache added where the number was read. This row is the DEFECT that invites it. A fix that bounds the producer's traversal discharges this row; a fix that caches the traversal discharges neither and files the other."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
